---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, link } from '../lib/site';
import { readBuild } from '../lib/data';
import { shortDate } from '../lib/format';

const build = readBuild();
---

<Base
  title={`About · ${SITE.name}`}
  description="What this catalogue is, where the data comes from, what it deliberately does not do, and how to run it yourself."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>What this is</h1>
      <p>
        Shelf is an independent, read-only catalogue of open-source applications that publish their builds as
        GitHub releases. It exists because those releases are public but not easy to browse: this site puts
        them on shelves by platform, recency and topic.
      </p>

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Not affiliated with Komi Store.</strong> This is a separate project. It uses the same public
        data the Komi Store app reads as its offline fallback, but it shares no branding, no code ownership
        and no support channel with that project. The name, the mark and this site belong to this project only.
      </div>

      <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p>
        The shelves are fetched at build time from the
        <a href={SITE.dataUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">komi-store-backend-data</a> mirror,
        the public fallback channel the app itself uses when its API is unreachable. Files sit on GitHub's
        static host, so this site never calls the app's API server.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>One shelf file per category, topic and platform.</li>
        <li>Records are deduplicated by repository id and ranked per shelf.</li>
        <li>Repository metadata (stars, releases, licence field) originates from GitHub itself.</li>
      </ul>
      {build && (
        <p>
          This build used {build.mirrors} shelf files and {build.repos.toLocaleString('en')} repositories, fetched on
          {' '}{shortDate(build.builtAt)}. Data therefore lags the mirror by one build.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2>What it does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No installs. Download links open the project's GitHub release page.</li>
        <li>No accounts, no favourites, no ratings, no tracking scripts.</li>
        <li>No live API. Everything you see is in the HTML of the page.</li>
        <li>No screenshots or README rendering. Those need the project API, which is not public from browsers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Licences and credit</h2>
      <p>
        Site code is MIT licensed. The mirrored data is published by the Komi Store project under
        Apache-2.0, and the underlying repository data belongs to GitHub and the individual projects.
        If you fork this catalogue, keep the attribution and do not imply endorsement by Komi Store.
      </p>

      <h2>Running it</h2>
      <p>
        The site is Astro with static output. Fetch the data, then build:
      </p>
      <pre>npm install
npm run data
npm run build</pre>
      <p>
        Source and issue tracker: <a href={SITE.sourceUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{SITE.sourceUrl}</a>.
        Something wrong with a project entry? Open an issue there, the data itself comes from the mirror.
      </p>
      <p><a href={link('')}>Back to the shelf</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
